    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d558">

                <pb facs="0552" n="380" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg380"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/980</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Fletcher</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-12-03T17:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 3, 1917, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received December 4, 3 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>600. My 552, November 8, 5 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d558-f1"/> The Mexican
                    delegation to the Buenos Aires conference is as follows: President and special
                    delegate, Luis Cabrera; special delegate, Gerzayn Ugarte; secretaries, Deputies
                    Flavio Perez Garza and Enrique Parra; military, Gen. Federico Montes; publicity
                    secretary, Ernesto Hidalgo; and two clerks.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fletcher</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
